# Trivy Ignore File for Catalogizer
# Format: CVE-ID # Justification
# Lines starting with # are comments

# Development/Testing files - not production code
# CVE-2023-1234 # Test dependency, not used in production

# False positives - vulnerabilities in code we don't use
# CVE-2022-5678 # Feature not enabled in our configuration

# Accepted risks - mitigated through other means
# CVE-2021-9999 # Mitigated by network isolation

# Development environment only
# The following only apply to development dependencies:

# Go module test dependencies
# These are only used in testing, not production builds

# Node.js devDependencies
# These are build tools, not runtime dependencies

# Documentation / Examples
# Vulnerabilities in example code that's not deployed

# NOTE: Add specific CVEs here with justifications as they are identified
# during security scans. Each entry MUST include a justification comment.
